{"abstract":"This dissertation in Science and Technology Studies (STS) examines the Danish Ministry of Education’s experiment, where, in the pursuit of making young people makers, not only users, of technology, and cultivating active participants in a digital democracy, a trial programme was launched to define, develop, trial, and evaluate a new, potentially mandatory, subject called ‘technology comprehension’ (teknologiforståelse) for the public school. This effort was both historical and politically consequential. Concerned with the politics of how technology education is assembled (‘critical Tech-Ed’), STS, ethnographic methods, and critical reading strategies are used to examine the relations and work of researchers, experts, teachers, and consultants. As well as the effects thereof. The thesis aims to understand what comes to be understood as affording technology comprehension and how; as well as what forms of knowing are negotiated and handled in the making of technology comprehension. The dissertation’s papers conceptualise knowledge-making as work of ‘discipline-ing’, translating, and prototyping. Discipline-ing is explored as an effect of the contents of the subject proposal for technology comprehension, which renders the world as digital building blocks that can be handled by the technologically educated person. Here, a technologically deterministic view dominates and limits how change and agency can be imagined. Translating is explored as the work of integrating design practice into technology comprehension learning, teaching, and subject matter development, as per the promise it is said to hold for ensuring the democratic and creative-constructive ideals of the public school. Translations of actors generate epistemic cultures, disciplinary canons, and perspectives on what constitutes good formative education, enacted, in particular, as a boundary between ‘theory’ and ‘practice’. Prototyping is explored through the proliferation of a prototyping culture, as pupils as well as teachers and subject matter developers engaged in prototyping and with prototypes. The capacity of prototyping is the handling of disparate social worlds, e.g. of epistemic uncertainty and of a ‘theory-practice divide’. The thesis highlights the relationality of knowledge-making in the trial programme. It also argues: that it is necessary and possible to imagine alternative relations with digital technology than those that reproduce a digital reality; for engaging the affordances of a theory-practice divide in the public school to develop technology comprehension; that the trial programme puts not only technology comprehension to the test in terms of its future as a school subject, but also tests the social fabric of postdigital Denmark, as it makes actors articulate their alliances to certain knowledges and methods. Relations that STS and critical Tech-Ed studies should engage and intervene in to make just, sustainable, and accountable educational and civic futures.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gahoonia, Simy Kaur"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730189"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"technology comprehension in the making discipline ing translating prototyping","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109068586/PhD_Thesis_Final_Version_Simy_Kaur.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Research funding by the Velux Foundations (PIs Vasilis Galis and Brit Ross Winthereik, project ID: 26584), and the IT University of Copenhagen."],"id":"S01-000.00-730189","ids":["itu-b173b415-b463-4a0c-a083-08f6e2d442d7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F7B3C5390F36A8720AA24B130B96625B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109068586/PhD_Thesis_Final_Version_Simy_Kaur.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simy Kaur","key":"gahooniapau","last":"Gahoonia","locid":"6c543b1d-8137-489d-b444-d17921fc9de9","name":"Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","orcid":"0000-0001-9668-6868","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"168","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b173b415-b463-4a0c-a083-08f6e2d442d7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Technology Comprehension In-The-Making : Discipline-ing, Translating, Prototyping","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730189","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper examines enactments of prototyping in a recent experimental effort to introduce ‘Technology Comprehension’ (TC) as a mandatory school subject in the Danish Public School. The overall concern of the programme was to educate young people to become not only users, but makers and analysts of the digital technological society. We adopt a social-theoretical view of prototyping that suggests it has moved well beyond design, and has become part of a broader cultural repertoire. We explore the capacity of prototyping as a site of social knowledge-production, illuminating prototypes as instruments of experimentation, epistemic negotiation, and civic participation. We analyse two prototypes: 1) an artefact that was the outcome of a pupil’s work in a TC lesson; 2) an experimental lesson plan called ‘App Design’ put to use by a teacher in a series of 5th grade TC lessons. Attending to how prototyping is performed in the pupils’, teachers’, and subject matter experts’ making, demoing, testing, and iterating on ‘first type’ tangible and material artefacts–prototypes. Prototyping in the trial programme can be understood as the rehearsal of chaotic conditions, in the teacher-pupil relation, and in the pupil-world relation. Prototyping can absorb the seeming impossibility of bridging ‘theoretical’ and ‘practical’ knowledges, and make new social and material agencies arise. The trial of TC seems in this light as much as an experiment in rendering social relations and knowledge-making, open-ended and experimental as it is an experiment in cultivating that exact attitude towards technology, but also towards societal affairs and knowledge-production.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776379"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Experimentation","Prototyping","School Education","Technology comprehension"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prototypes all the way down prototyping in the teaching and development of technology comprehension","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/stse.v16i1.145136","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776379","ids":["itu-23a31dba-bcc9-448a-abe6-4b7352357527"],"keyword":["Experimentation","Prototyping","School education","Subject matter development","Technology comprehension"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-BD4627752EE7321B8274B9A696A25214"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/stse.v16i1.145136","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/encounters/article/view/145136/188386","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simy Kaur","key":"gahooniapau","last":"Gahoonia","locid":"6c543b1d-8137-489d-b444-d17921fc9de9","name":"Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","orcid":"0000-0001-9668-6868","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/stse.v16i1.145136","issn":["19044372"],"issue":"1","journal":"STS Encounters","pages":"3-18","publisher":"Danish Association for Science and Technology Studies","status":"p","title":"STS Encounters","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-23a31dba-bcc9-448a-abe6-4b7352357527"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prototypes all the way down : Prototyping in the teaching and development of technology Comprehension","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776379","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Whilst STS has long studied lab work, the past few years have also seen the introduction of labs as social formations for doing STS enquiry. But what kind of contributions to pedagogy, particularly in technical universities, can STS inspired university labs make? We respond to the need to more deeply understand how teaching may be practiced as a site of STS experimentation by describing the work of the ETHOS Lab, our critical feminist lab at the IT University of Copenhagen, as ‘enlivening’. Using three events from 2017–2020 as case studies, we identify both the use of space and shaping of time as integral to how we have sought to trouble knowledge production in our own environment, particularly by creating sites and situations where teaching and research cannot be separated. By showing how our Lab activities intervene in ways of knowing and doing within university hierarchies and cultures, we aim to contribute an analysis of the critical potential of STS lab work in technical environments, and recommendations from our situated evolving space of feminist praxis within an interdisciplinary IT University.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Douglas-Jones, Rachel","Cakici, Baki","Cohn, Marisa","Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","Ojala, Mace","Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789556"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ruhr University Bochum"],"keyword":["Computer Science","Feminist pedagogy","LAB","Placemaking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spaceships and poetry enlivening the lab as a site of feminist critical pedagogy","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17351/ests2023.1915","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789556","ids":["itu-711e4444-5f30-43d1-96a7-2c354602ea71"],"keyword":["computer science","feminist pedagogy","lab","placemaking","timework"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C15951B8EA8B501240253FD3148DCFAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17351/ests2023.1915","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"https://estsjournal.org/index.php/ests/article/view/1915/815","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ruhr university bochum","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ruhr University Bochum","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","locid":"b614ac6f-eefa-44a3-8b9a-092b88d86d37","name":"Cakici, Baki","orcid":"0000-0002-1039-8177","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simy Kaur","key":"gahooniapau","last":"Gahoonia","locid":"6c543b1d-8137-489d-b444-d17921fc9de9","name":"Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","orcid":"0000-0001-9668-6868","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mace","key":"ojalapau","last":"Ojala","name":"Ojala, Mace","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cæcilie Sloth","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"3ef9211c-34b2-4061-ba59-c5800d6a5b32","name":"Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth","orcid":"0000-0001-7102-7268","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.17351/ests2023.1915","issn":["24138053"],"issue":"1-2","journal":"Engaging Science, Technology, and Society","publisher":"Society for Social Studies of Science","status":"p","title":"Engaging Science, Technology, and Society","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-711e4444-5f30-43d1-96a7-2c354602ea71"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Spaceships and Poetry : Enlivening the Lab as a site of Feminist Critical Pedagogy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789556","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper directs attention to a recent government-led school development initiative in Denmark, where a broad concept and practice of design became central to imagining and reworking technology education for the postdigital condition, in which schoolchildren were imagined to become makers, not users of technological society. Using an analytical apparatus inspired by Science and Technology Studies (STS), the paper examines how and what understandings of design were propagated in the trial of technology comprehension in the public school. The paper examines two design models as didactic-pedagogical translation of design into the epistemic practices of the public school, articulated in the intellectual traditions of Bildung and Didaktik. Examining the knowledges that make knowledges, the paper contributes an elucidation of the features, capacities, and limitations of the concept and practice of design, as it is mobilised to make knowledge and subjectivities about agency and change for schooling in the postdigital educational future.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gahoonia, Simy Kaur"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712545"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design","Education","Inscriptions","Mattering","Postdigital","Technology comprehension"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"makers not users inscriptions of design in the development of postdigital technology education","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s42438-023-00431-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712545","identifier":[{"id":"85174482998","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a5e7fcc2-f1f7-4386-a73b-2fbd9b6aa5fc"],"keyword":["Design","Education","Inscriptions","Mattering","Postdigital","Technology comprehension"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-02F2CE18E337DC0C7BDC2B1571F66DD6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s42438-023-00431-7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s42438-023-00431-7","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simy Kaur","key":"gahooniapau","last":"Gahoonia","locid":"6c543b1d-8137-489d-b444-d17921fc9de9","name":"Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","orcid":"0000-0001-9668-6868","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s42438-023-00431-7","issn":["2524485X","25244868"],"issn_org":["2524485X"],"journal":"Postdigital Science and Education","pages":"98-113","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Postdigital Science and Education","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174482998"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a5e7fcc2-f1f7-4386-a73b-2fbd9b6aa5fc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Makers, Not Users: Inscriptions of Design in the Development of Postdigital Technology Education","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712545","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This paper explores how the Danish school sector currently performs and reworks students’ engagement with digitalization through prototyping. Public schooling is routinely mobilized by the state as part of the solution to perceived societal problems. By law, Danish schooling should prepare students for participation, co-responsibility, rights, and duties in a democratic society. Recently, this includes preparing students for life in an increasingly digitalized democracy. We investigate the Ministry of Children and Education’s trial of ‘technology comprehension’ (2018-2021). This was an experimental effort to determine how to introduce ‘understanding of technology’ into compulsory schooling as a generally formative, creativeconstructive, and critical subject matter combining societal reflection, computer science and design approaches. The curriculum suggested that design approaches, especially, were conducive to agency and empowerment in digital democratic life, making it imperative that students learn to materialize digital artifacts through prototyping. This takes prototyping beyond its traditional use in design and systems development, making experimentalism central to the conduct of citizenship and social life. We examine prototyping across the trial: the curriculum; the trial’s design; the classroom; and the trial’s evaluation. We argue that prototyping functions as a device for intervention in the complexity and uncertainty of a digital democratic future. In this situation, the capacity of prototyping is to keep matters of concern both open and closed across scales, and bind different sites of the trial together. We critically examine the role of the prototype in a democracy in ’perpetual beta’ and the response: educating students to cultivate a design attitude.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776437"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design based learning","Digital literacy","Prototyping","Technology comprehension"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prototyping the future prototyping citizens the trial of technology comprehension in danish schooling","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-776437","ids":["itu-abe568dd-605c-419f-8b00-3fbdfa39be6e"],"keyword":["Democratic citizenship in education","Design-based learning","Digital literacy","Prototyping","Technology comprehension"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E2CDC10E25C8F98888043029AAAA139B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simy Kaur","key":"gahooniapau","last":"Gahoonia","locid":"6c543b1d-8137-489d-b444-d17921fc9de9","name":"Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","orcid":"0000-0001-9668-6868","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-abe568dd-605c-419f-8b00-3fbdfa39be6e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prototyping the future, prototyping citizens: The trial of Technology Comprehension in Danish Schooling","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776437","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we suggest approaching writing as a vulnerable practice marked by an unstable boundary between bodies: bodies of text and bodies of writers. We present an exercise-method that we refer to as Monster Writing, which we have developed in order to engage with these instabilities as well as in order to address experiences of difficulty, anxiety and uncertainty in relation with the text and writing process. Though the writing process can at times be exciting and thrilling, and at other times perhaps a little tedious and mundane, for some it also presents (more than) occasional encounters with one's own insecurities, shame and doubt. We argue that this potentially more painful relationship between writer and text should be awarded more attention in scholarship on writing, and that a way of doing so is through the framework of feminist theory on vulnerability, embodiment, and the monstrous.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Henriksen, Line","Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","Blønd, Marie","Cohn, Marisa","Cakici, Baki","Douglas-Jones, Rachel","Ferreira, Pedro","Feshak, Viktoriya","Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","Sandbukt, Sunniva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383081"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technical University of Munich"],"keyword":["Feminist theory","Monster theory","Organizational studies","Vulnerability","Writing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"writing bodies and bodies of text thinking vulnerability through monsters","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/gwao.12782","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383081","identifier":[{"id":"85121653378","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7b7818dc-cf90-442f-826c-fe4264251f64"],"keyword":["feminist theory","monster theory","organizational studies","vulnerability","writing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5993E6636350380725B0F7E6033835DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/gwao.12782","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/gwao.12782","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Meldgaard","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"0c46864b-a7f8-4439-aeda-0781f77bfe88","name":"Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7994-5186","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"bløndpau","last":"Blønd","name":"Blønd, Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","locid":"b614ac6f-eefa-44a3-8b9a-092b88d86d37","name":"Cakici, Baki","orcid":"0000-0002-1039-8177","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","locid":"1b3cff7f-1549-4998-b52e-0ba9093e1d01","name":"Ferreira, Pedro","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Viktoriya","key":"feshakpau","last":"Feshak","name":"Feshak, Viktoriya","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simy Kaur","key":"gahooniapau","last":"Gahoonia","locid":"6c543b1d-8137-489d-b444-d17921fc9de9","name":"Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","orcid":"0000-0001-9668-6868","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sunniva","key":"sandbuktpau","last":"Sandbukt","locid":"06d038a4-f659-4c53-8a6d-58e295ab603f","name":"Sandbukt, Sunniva","orcid":"0009-0002-4274-4991","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/gwao.12782","issn":["09686673","14680432"],"issn_org":["09686673"],"journal":"Gender, Work and Organization","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Gender, Work and Organization"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121653378"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7b7818dc-cf90-442f-826c-fe4264251f64"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Writing bodies and bodies of text: Thinking vulnerability through monsters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383081","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"On the eve of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) coming into effect we, a university laboratory, marked the occasion with an interactive installation called Compliance. Data traces from Compliance were subsequently processed by the lab, here enacted in the form of a play. While much discussion has centered around modern 'black-boxed' processing of data, less attention has been paid to the value of the data itself, and whether it merits use. We draw on dramaturgical methods for both analysis and presentation [15], allowing for readers to imagine staging their own, different, versions of the event. Drawing on the ambiguous ontological status of (yet unexamined) data, we offer a discussion on the value of data, its use and non-use, as well as how to live with this ambivalence, continuously negotiating social contracts about our further conduct with the data.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","Ferreira, Pedro","Cohn, Marisa","Henriksen, Line","Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","Hockenhull, Michael","Cakici, Baki","Blønd, Marie","Douglas-Jones, Rachel","Laursen, Cæcilie Sloth","Zell, Sonja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384849"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["GDPR","data non use","dramaturgical methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"upon not opening the black box","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85090243080","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384849","identifier":[{"id":"85090243080","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f39b7fd5-7493-4bf3-a0f8-14dc03ecc282"],"keyword":["GDPR","data non-use","dramaturgical methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-276723FEC91BFD0CA307B03D82CF6C55"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simy Kaur","key":"gahooniapau","last":"Gahoonia","locid":"6c543b1d-8137-489d-b444-d17921fc9de9","name":"Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","orcid":"0000-0001-9668-6868","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","locid":"1b3cff7f-1549-4998-b52e-0ba9093e1d01","name":"Ferreira, Pedro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Line","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Meldgaard","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"0c46864b-a7f8-4439-aeda-0781f77bfe88","name":"Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7994-5186","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"hockenhullpau","last":"Hockenhull","locid":"5041f387-908f-4845-9f79-3a6dbd527f4b","name":"Hockenhull, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-2670-2102","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","locid":"b614ac6f-eefa-44a3-8b9a-092b88d86d37","name":"Cakici, Baki","orcid":"0000-0002-1039-8177","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","